config APEX_RADIO_KEYBOARD_EVENT_RX
    bool "Wake the keyboard radio thread on packet reception"
    default n
    depends on APEX_G4B_RADIO_INPUT && APEX_RADIO_HOPPING
    help
      Route RADIO END through the PPI channel 17 fork to EGU3. This uses
      SWI3/EGU3 instead of replacing Bluetooth's direct RADIO interrupt.
      Enabled only after Bluetooth shutdown; incompatible with another EGU3
      or nrfx software-interrupt user.

config APEX_RADIO_TEST_CHANNEL
    int "Fixed radio test channel (MHz above 2400)"
    range 0 80
    default 40
    help
      Both devices must use the same value. This selects a single frequency
      for development measurements; it does not enable channel hopping.

config APEX_RADIO_HOPPING
    bool "Experimental timed channel hopping"
    default n
    depends on APEX_G4B_RADIO_INPUT || APEX_RECEIVER_RADIO_INPUT
    help
      Negotiate a session-bound channel map and hop in 20 ms slots. Owns
      TIMER2 and PPI channels 17 and 18 after Bluetooth has shut down.
      Requires matching keyboard and receiver builds. Not a 1 kHz scheduler.
